# One card (TP=1): read by serve.sh after radiance.env and overriding it. These are the lines in
# which the 0.9.3 launcher's single-GPU profile (serve-mxfp4.sh, SINGLE_GPU_PROFILE) gives its
# container different values than at TP=2; captured from its dry runs on 2026-11-23. The profile's
# vLLM options (16-bit mamba state, capture sizes, the batch shape) are set by serve.sh.
#
# The fused GDN decode step is routed by (sequences x v-heads) <= this. One card holds all 48
# v-heads, so 32 (one sequence at TP=2's 24 heads) would never take it; measured 37.0 us fused
# against 48.3 for the pair at one sequence (serve-mxfp4.sh, 2026-09-16).
RADIANCE_GDN_FUSED_MAX_ITEMS=48
